Description:

Rolling replication, and sync_client ``-N``, no longer wait for a locked
user or mailbox.  The work is written back to the sync log and retried on
the next pass, so one long-running lock (such as a reconstruct) no longer
holds up replication of every other user.  This now also works for the
default sync log channel, not just a channel named with ``-n``.  With
``-N``, the ``-u`` and ``-m`` modes now skip a locked user or mailbox, as
``-A`` already did, instead of reporting an error.


